[1.0] PRODUCT INFORMATION
=========================
Name.........: ZAddFile
Version......: 1.0
This release.: 23-Apr-95
First release: 23-Apr-95


[1.1] WHAT IS THIS?
===================
Crap? :-) With this little utility you can mark files on the HD for a
user online. If you don't specify a file to mark ZAddFile will open a
multiselect file requester.


[1.2] QUICK INTRODUCTION
========================
This is for doc haters (I'm one of them:). Ok, to get the idea
type "ZAddFile NODE=<A node with a user online>" in a shell. You can
also try "ZAddFile NODE=<A node with a user online> FILE=<A file>".

You can also use these keywords as tool types in ZAddFiles's icon.


[1.3] WARNING
=============
As far as I can see Zeus can't handle paths/file names with
space in, so ZAddFile won't let you mark such files until this
is sorted out.

I.e. you can't mark files in RAM: since ZAddFile will expand RAM: to
"Ram Disk:".


[1.4] REQUIREMENTS
==================
In order to use this program you need:

   o An Amiga.

   o AmigaDOS 2.04 or higher.

   o Zeus Professional BBS system.

   o A user online.


[1.5] FEATURES
==============
   o Can be launched from a shell, Workbench, one of the ANSI watcher's
     keys etc.

   o Supports both arguments from cli and Workbench, through tool types.

   o If you don't specify a file ZAddFile will open a multiselect
     file requester.

   o Several files can be marked (Not without the file requester).

   o Puts the screen, where the file requester is, to front.

   o Made by Centauri Software (What? OF COURSE it's a feature!;).


[1.6] INSTALATION
=================
o Copy ZAddFile anywhere.

Optional:
o Run an ANSI watcher.
o Click on the "Keys" gadget and select an empty string.
o Write "<Full path to ZAddFile> NODE=%n"
o Select Control->Save Config in the menu.


[1.7] USAGE
===========
ZAddFile supports to arguments, "NODE" and "FILE". However these
are optional. The default node is 0 and if you don't specify a
file ZAddFile will open a asl file requester on the ANSI watcher
screen or default public screen.

This file requester is capable of selecting several files, which are
in the same directory. Press a shift key while selecting files and
you'll see.

ZAddFile can also be used from the workbench. Both keywords can be
used as tool types in ZAddFile's icon.


[1.8] EXAMPLES
==============
From a shell:
ZAddFile
ZAddFile FILE=RAM:ForYou.lzx
ZAddFile NODE=1
ZAddFile NODE=2 FILE=S:Startup-sequence

From Workbench (Icon's tool types):
<nothing>
NODE=1
NODE=1 FILE=S:Startup-sequence
FILE=S:Startup-sequence

From an ANSI watcher key:
Zeus:Bin/ZAddFile NODE=%n
Zeus:Bin/ZAddFile NODE=%n FILE=S:Startup-sequence


